{"body":{"model":"haiku","reads":{"$ref":"01M6S09BX5DDBXFS8D3EQZG0QR"},"seedFrom":"inside","top":{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMPQ0JHAM49KZAEKE61"},"understandings":[{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMPQ0JHAM49KZAEKE61"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR2P302EHMA19CYRXF"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRPWYJTDB1K4NMCTC5"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR8JGQTKRZBPNTVDAZ"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR707M07B9B4609F83"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRSYEFZWC5VRPCY1X4"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRVEY7D3YTDZNZ63JC"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRZFN77T7878QZ49PQ"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRJXTF81DDP2N2EBF1"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRK87BJMGT9DJFS2ZK"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR4FKQT9569Z66CWC8"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR8YSJ0PWGP1GM1GNZ"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR2DDXNY1H9GHS7MFN"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRT90AAKC3V32VAZM0"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRJ5H8KZ3PGGH7YZ2D"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRTN4NCTFFCFWY7R1F"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRQTQ93B0PJ0TXJB90"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR0YPB5FME83PNEYB3"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR0QB63TAB88JTZNS5"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRFTBV4W7PATMGSYVH"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRETDYS94XKXNDA3NT"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMREXK403CYFDJ6AG58"}]},"id":"01M6SD2EMREKG6QK59DR9ZC3Y9","instance":["01M6S74NG0JR8Q2S499AF7FR71"],"kind":"version","name":"branch-11","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"how much coherence is reached without central control, and whether the proposal stays conceptual or is tested","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR2P302EHMA19CYRXF"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRPWYJTDB1K4NMCTC5"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR8JGQTKRZBPNTVDAZ"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR707M07B9B4609F83"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRSYEFZWC5VRPCY1X4"},{"$ref":"01M6S09BKTDMZ0B76G7C8BX946"},{"$ref":"01M6S09BX3RAPV03PXJHMR2Z5K"}],"prose":"The whole reads as a proposal to extend holonic systems so that they hold ethical, effective, understanding, unbiased and vigilant roles, coordinated by one federating holon, and then to test that arrangement in simulation and in a single transport setting. It stays a conceptual framework that is argued for rather than measured.","title":"A holarchy that trades pure efficiency for coordination"},"id":"01M6SD2EMPQ0JHAM49KZAEKE61","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"how nested autonomy is bounded by position in the hierarchy","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRVEY7D3YTDZNZ63JC"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRZFN77T7878QZ49PQ"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRJXTF81DDP2N2EBF1"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRK87BJMGT9DJFS2ZK"}],"prose":"Before any new role is added, the paper rests on what a holon is: a whole that is also a part, nested in levels of autonomy, with a lineage that began in manufacturing and spread outward. The pressures that make autonomous systems fall short are set against that ground as the reason for change.","title":"The holon as ground"},"id":"01M6SD2EMR2P302EHMA19CYRXF","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"the balance between local freedom and directives from above","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S08ZK9JNT733QPVPKKPB33"},{"$ref":"01M6S08ZQJDTPV1K5MVEQB7EKC"}],"prose":"A holon is autonomous in its own scope yet bound by the level above it, so authority is spread across the tiers instead of concentrated at the top. Local decisions align with system objectives through that bounded autonomy.","title":"Nested autonomy within a hierarchy"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRVEY7D3YTDZNZ63JC","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"the domain in which holarchy is applied and the kind of control it replaces","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S090806VNZVA97AV0V0XD2"},{"$ref":"01M6S090GX8FSDRJ0E4TJ1H3DX"},{"$ref":"01M6S090PDBF0YZFN6YMV9WJ5W"}],"prose":"The idea starts with a philosophical notion of entities working at several levels at once, is taken up in production systems for flexibility against centralised control, and then spreads into smart grids, construction and cyber-physical work. Each step keeps the holarchy but changes the domain it serves.","title":"Lineage from manufacturing outward"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRZFN77T7878QZ49PQ","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"which failure mode is treated as the most serious gap","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S08YV85BZVM4G694CQKMYX"},{"$ref":"01M6S08Z79ESR6PT11B13KVPB3"},{"$ref":"01M6S0912JT6RA5BZ9DA4QWXW0"}],"prose":"Autonomous systems are described as brittle under change, prone to bias, short of accountability and thin on shared awareness. These are offered as the gaps the holonic extension is meant to close, and the case rests on them.","title":"Limits of autonomous systems as the spur"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRJXTF81DDP2N2EBF1","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"how much live data a holon can draw on while staying locally autonomous","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S0916BHS51YPSAGK594MMT"},{"$ref":"01M6S0919HQTTW5K4S0JD9BAN6"},{"$ref":"01M6S091CAZDYVGXTAQ2RARAAA"},{"$ref":"01M6S091KTFAT80JBWTQHERM05"}],"prose":"Digital twins, federated learning and AI models are presented as a way to give holons live data, fault tolerance and self-optimisation. The remedy is argued as compatible with holonic autonomy rather than as a replacement for it.","title":"AI and twins as a remedy"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRK87BJMGT9DJFS2ZK","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"which failure of a narrow optimiser each role is meant to answer","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR4FKQT9569Z66CWC8"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR8YSJ0PWGP1GM1GNZ"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR2DDXNY1H9GHS7MFN"}],"prose":"The paper names five roles a holon can take on, each answering a particular failure of efficiency-first autonomy. Two of them pull against each other, three concern what a holon knows and how it watches, and every one of them carries its own difficulties in definition.","title":"Five dimensions as roles"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRPWYJTDB1K4NMCTC5","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"how a value is weighed when the short-term and long-term or the fair and the fast disagree","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S093679WVYX9W76WMQSFYF"},{"$ref":"01M6S093JWWSFCKGZGR3EF21M7"},{"$ref":"01M6S093NFQRR88X9PD990GSFB"},{"$ref":"01M6S0950DPJQCE6FKYH7TSD58"},{"$ref":"01M6S097S811FX4ENN201BA6PM"}],"prose":"Ethical holons and effective holons are set as a balancing pair: one guards fairness and safety, the other looks past short-term efficiency to sustainability and long-run outcomes. The two are expected to meet in negotiation rather than in a single rule.","title":"Ethics weighed against effectiveness"},"id":"01M6SD2EMR4FKQT9569Z66CWC8","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"the fidelity of what a holon knows and how far that knowledge is shared","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S093YQ6AXJZ5BM1HF4WFQX"},{"$ref":"01M6S0949YC2RGE7SVC8VQ2BJA"},{"$ref":"01M6S094NQQR6J9EGV6K49FTZS"},{"$ref":"01M6S0951AZ5JE4ABRCQSXWQ2F"},{"$ref":"01M6S0953BG3WSGDTSRPS30552"}],"prose":"Three roles concern what a holon knows and how it watches. Understanding is structured knowledge, unbiased is a check against distortion in that knowledge, and vigilance is shared awareness across holons that keeps local views from drifting away from the whole.","title":"Understanding, bias and vigilance as knowing"},"id":"01M6SD2EMR8YSJ0PWGP1GM1GNZ","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"whether the criteria for a role can be written down precisely enough to be checked","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S093FSPTEATFTYCNEJEMQ4"},{"$ref":"01M6S093W4DZ6B9GKDGMNA5DED"},{"$ref":"01M6S09474K3F10PRDVM1JZJ06"},{"$ref":"01M6S094H6M3N8CRFWQ98BWV6P"},{"$ref":"01M6S094K282XW4C3DANB6FYG7"},{"$ref":"01M6S094XMKX1YC7SH2K1A4ZDZ"}],"prose":"The paper's own challenge lists show a recurring edge: a role cannot be implemented until its criteria are written down, whether those are ethical guidelines, effectiveness metrics, ontologies or bias patterns. The difficulty is less in the concept than in fixing what counts as success.","title":"Where each role gets hard to define"},"id":"01M6SD2EMR2DDXNY1H9GHS7MFN","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"the degree of autonomy a holon holds over the run it is part of","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRT90AAKC3V32VAZM0"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRJ5H8KZ3PGGH7YZ2D"}],"prose":"Simulation is recast so that holons are both the entities being simulated and the agents that steer the run. The section sorts the ways this can happen by how much autonomy the holons hold, and argues that the directing role is a new step beyond agent-based simulation.","title":"Holons that direct their own simulation"},"id":"01M6SD2EMR8JGQTKRZBPNTVDAZ","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"how far a holon may alter the rules or objectives of the simulation it sits in","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S091PP1ZZQG6WZ7R3BMA7Q"},{"$ref":"01M6S091YM28K8SWNXGQD94QWR"},{"$ref":"01M6S092GHEZCKHBE4ZKEW3J78"},{"$ref":"01M6S092MRCB5DHW2QJWZCMH6P"},{"$ref":"01M6S092NT1X7H7BGXEJM161WB"},{"$ref":"01M6S092PS96FXNTYW0G07YCMZ"},{"$ref":"01M6S092QP2J2DR6DJZ6E197EW"}],"prose":"Agent-directed simulation is taken over and sorted into passive, reactive, adaptive and proactive forms of holon-directed simulation, ordered by how much a holon may change the rules or objectives of a run. The sort follows the paper's own categories.","title":"A taxonomy of holon-directed simulation"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRT90AAKC3V32VAZM0","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"what distinguishes a holon acting in a run from an agent acting in one","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S092GHEZCKHBE4ZKEW3J78"},{"$ref":"01M6S092RHVP4CPW8DAZR8Q3QP"},{"$ref":"01M6S092RXW7KF4BQKGGRPEJTG"},{"$ref":"01M6S092TSGGXA8WG36SRK5TND"},{"$ref":"01M6S092XTJ4DM3B12H6CFN807"},{"$ref":"01M6S09BPKS0KGT7SR4GE75ACB"}],"prose":"The paper claims holon-directed simulation as a first formal use of the term and as a natural extension of agent-based work, with requirements for real-time adaptation and coordination. The claim is made largely by argument and analogy rather than by a worked method.","title":"Holon-directed simulation as a new step"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRJ5H8KZ3PGGH7YZ2D","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"how far alignment can be negotiated at runtime rather than fixed in advance","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRTN4NCTFFCFWY7R1F"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRQTQ93B0PJ0TXJB90"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR0YPB5FME83PNEYB3"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMR0QB63TAB88JTZNS5"}],"prose":"A single federated interoperability holon is proposed to hold the other holons together without a shared model or central authority. Its barriers, its modes of alignment, its functions, its component architecture and its open costs make up the bulk of the contribution.","title":"The federating holon that binds the rest"},"id":"01M6SD2EMR707M07B9B4609F83","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"whether a shared representation layer is imposed or left out","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S0957APBWA2W6N7RK4HA1J"},{"$ref":"01M6S095GRG93K5EG2K71B1CKV"},{"$ref":"01M6S095HBYZ649HND3ZYXDXYT"},{"$ref":"01M6S095HYCF58A43XBQ8GAQ7Q"},{"$ref":"01M6S095KGFWMBWNW19K2CKDZC"},{"$ref":"01M6S095PBA4ZRBXY1GY14VWHR"},{"$ref":"01M6S095Q6V5YHG5EJ40PT2KHP"},{"$ref":"01M6S095RQV1YWJ0PTP40VJPNM"}],"prose":"Interoperability is broken into conceptual, organisational and technical barriers, spread across data, service, process and business concerns, and then sorted into integrated, unified and federated approaches. The federated mode is singled out as the one that lets systems keep their own models.","title":"Barriers and modes of interoperability"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRTN4NCTFFCFWY7R1F","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"how long an alignment lives and how much of a holon's internals it must expose","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S095WN23Y8DRJGK8C24NJV"},{"$ref":"01M6S09654M23DFDXTHS52MBXA"},{"$ref":"01M6S096NJ1YCGW3GT69CTCK3B"},{"$ref":"01M6S096SSRKHN58F6YBT2PD3S"},{"$ref":"01M6S099046TN4NZCBCFH60P0M"},{"$ref":"01M6S0992KZHB02ZBDX260T244"},{"$ref":"01M6S0997JNB7G6FJ23GTB226M"}],"prose":"Federated interoperability is treated as something settled while the system runs, through short-lived ontologies, schema mapping and negotiated interfaces. The holon keeps its internal logic, and only the mediation between holons is dynamic.","title":"Alignment negotiated at runtime"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRQTQ93B0PJ0TXJB90","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"how much of the connective work is delegated to language-model components versus fixed graph structures","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S09710AV583QD1MPBPW32H"},{"$ref":"01M6S097JQCMENMDG4DXR4V4ZJ"},{"$ref":"01M6S097N1AM8EGG88P63ZS8D9"},{"$ref":"01M6S0982Y69VFJ6C8NQBP89NE"},{"$ref":"01M6S0988S3MZFMVE7H1RCZSJZ"},{"$ref":"01M6S098BNS851MZHX3SFT2NYC"},{"$ref":"01M6S098ECD82QGT0KGXZG1EAS"},{"$ref":"01M6S098FH9YH6FMBTFF272DJA"},{"$ref":"01M6S098GRA69D8E61BGJ3ETJF"},{"$ref":"01M6S098HDWNMXMGHDKP7HYH0G"},{"$ref":"01M6S098M0RG9CGW3VBAQ8E35X"}],"prose":"The federating holon brokers communication, aligns goals, arbitrates conflict and reconfigures roles. It is then broken into six components, an orchestrator at the top and an integrator, translator, element finder and workflow pair beneath it, some of which can be left out.","title":"What the federating holon does and is made of"},"id":"01M6SD2EMR0YPB5FME83PNEYB3","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"which cost, whether standards, latency, or trust, binds first as the system grows","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S096929EE6AD520SWDPK4N"},{"$ref":"01M6S0974ESZ3BC4PQGRAQ140D"},{"$ref":"01M6S0976Z3XG1JS1A2VTTTBZN"},{"$ref":"01M6S0978GWDT0ZWN8XT22K2EJ"},{"$ref":"01M6S098NTTHF9ESCJ8CYMNPR9"},{"$ref":"01M6S098Q89NK293FCZ3EYNTNC"},{"$ref":"01M6S098WFFJ09R57JCXQAZAM3"},{"$ref":"01M6S098YF407XTYGG61RBEPZ7"}],"prose":"Standardisation, scale, security and privacy, and cross-domain governance are named as obstacles that stand in front of the federating holon. Blockchain and AI conflict anticipation are offered as possible answers, without being built.","title":"Costs the federating holon has not yet paid"},"id":"01M6SD2EMR0QB63TAB88JTZNS5","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"whether the setting is a demonstration of applicability or a measured result","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRFTBV4W7PATMGSYVH"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMRETDYS94XKXNDA3NT"},{"$ref":"01M6SD2EMREXK403CYFDJ6AG58"}],"prose":"A rural transport setting is chosen to show the framework working: the holons are mapped onto travellers, services and monitors, and the federated run is described step by step. The case is offered as an instance of the concepts, not as a validation.","title":"Rural mobility as the test field"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRSYEFZWC5VRPCY1X4","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"the spatial gaps in transport that the system is meant to expose","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S099CXGHQV3WHYC9KRGE4P"},{"$ref":"01M6S099H77DWSEH2T534Q8NP8"},{"$ref":"01M6S099K16DKC7EQQ35ANCYXH"},{"$ref":"01M6S099P1AJBBMKJ6BC76WM36"},{"$ref":"01M6S099QDK964CYS5R06EN4WT"},{"$ref":"01M6S099RX7Z7ZGC575Z0RX8W5"}],"prose":"Rural mobility is framed as a problem that central planning serves badly, and the platform is meant to reveal where no transport exists at all. The functions listed are data collection, interoperation, desert discovery, adaptation and simulation.","title":"The rural case and the transit desert"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRFTBV4W7PATMGSYVH","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"the order of requests and updates and who holds authority at each step","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S09A2TPJHK2PYS75HJWY0Y"},{"$ref":"01M6S09A5WEFJY26M01RF4RE1F"},{"$ref":"01M6S09AB69C8H307DTGBZQJX3"},{"$ref":"01M6S09AG184GYEQ79ZCXADC7B"},{"$ref":"01M6S09BAGXSGTE19VJ36NDS5M"},{"$ref":"01M6S09BD7Q7DNEGX5EB0MJ8HK"}],"prose":"The mapping walks through one trip: the federating holon starts the federation, travellers ask, services answer with routes and prices, monitors feed in conditions, and the loop closes with validation and a report back to the user. Reports about avoided zones are also sent upward for planning.","title":"Holons in the mobility loop"},"id":"01M6SD2EMRETDYS94XKXNDA3NT","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"matters":"how errors are caught and whether the results loop back into the system's own strategies","parts":[{"$ref":"01M6S09AH0YMYNDBY3FA44T68F"},{"$ref":"01M6S09AXT9RAEXAGQP942K710"},{"$ref":"01M6S09B0KJPXKB931FZC1JHE3"},{"$ref":"01M6S09B4PEE2MM0G40XAMDENJ"}],"prose":"The simulation is built on an HLA runtime, with federates standing in for the travellers, services and federating holon, and a federation manager that flags and invalidates faulty results. The run ends with a performance analysis of time, emissions and access.","title":"The federation run through HLA"},"id":"01M6SD2EMREXK403CYFDJ6AG58","instance":["01M6S74NG13VF3EH1MBDYGSKMZ"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"depth":6,"kind":"index-leaf","versions":{"01M6SD2EMPQ0JHAM49KZAEKE61":"sha256-a315251db188e434fd40b683219586c653fae5b16567133b113046e128c3b4de","01M6SD2EMR0QB63TAB88JTZNS5":"sha256-13a4f2021c59563cc3fa9ae89c6e8687c18fe14e31330972a5b618176d5cfa0d","01M6SD2EMR0YPB5FME83PNEYB3":"sha256-57999d7edd0061c265914446c5fb13006e07e9554ac8bf9cbd4f98977391664e","01M6SD2EMR2DDXNY1H9GHS7MFN":"sha256-1a90c55f1decf375dd14955a35c52e64d7163f99b288a5eaedade15b247af38a","01M6SD2EMR2P302EHMA19CYRXF":"sha256-81547fd36875ffd14d07d0685588aa3adfd7f7ddf5a7ec1e9c647d28069cbaa7","01M6SD2EMR4FKQT9569Z66CWC8":"sha256-c299f762d085cfadec87472a4005c27f7ab1e2286744b47c44d8fafc98738f44","01M6SD2EMR707M07B9B4609F83":"sha256-db157f47d923816bda8e797ae6cd53dcb6800eec38a1088135de5ded91a167ae","01M6SD2EMR8JGQTKRZBPNTVDAZ":"sha256-280cdebc48fc5b349452f2a608ef85744460443a8ee579a7f81b9fadfb7dce14","01M6SD2EMR8YSJ0PWGP1GM1GNZ":"sha256-9b69d573ab370c5cfda1c6016eeed38efc9e5eb60989be8faa53ef72b551ea1c","01M6SD2EMREKG6QK59DR9ZC3Y9":"sha256-10d0ac6e6bed42c25034398e3ee4d161aefcf287f256ff74fde49f1f00be6b44","01M6SD2EMRETDYS94XKXNDA3NT":"sha256-071ad34f11d23eeb8e3f0826494a3684973e4065aea80ae0f4cbb649731e6686","01M6SD2EMREXK403CYFDJ6AG58":"sha256-05a3089ffe25ab031e70b7c6ae3f2b3dcd80d41a1081f3b14a0e90e69fbadb55","01M6SD2EMRFTBV4W7PATMGSYVH":"sha256-fb0308ca2e6a0a12f7ed82ee1faf5b339901ffd222a63a9e977f90da93045898","01M6SD2EMRJ5H8KZ3PGGH7YZ2D":"sha256-55bee7020896838a7500d7b1f1e4677ae8654751acc71b4238d6a4c62b029d39","01M6SD2EMRJXTF81DDP2N2EBF1":"sha256-75b3e07a5727d7c7bce93db168dc6c3b1566485dc0faab14caa066c48f5f63e6","01M6SD2EMRK87BJMGT9DJFS2ZK":"sha256-708d68084356e385293afe2a37e53ade8e3beb426ea7b75430eed0ff73f85c38","01M6SD2EMRPWYJTDB1K4NMCTC5":"sha256-2bd545a98a9611ef4c462454d46ce7466f8ebca2c503a1d43cb525ccf52b55d2","01M6SD2EMRQTQ93B0PJ0TXJB90":"sha256-935a7e0c5021ca3dd60376fc9af5bd662b3db38a59fa99c40481eb426f68de93","01M6SD2EMRSYEFZWC5VRPCY1X4":"sha256-3455ca0f1f5751ca7ca12acc5e4ee5f55a459b676155bc5c45b04d05f16fbda5","01M6SD2EMRT90AAKC3V32VAZM0":"sha256-577fd97db277424e7fcb6306656c1e6ce171b092c12443598e30798b0ee84b9f","01M6SD2EMRTN4NCTFFCFWY7R1F":"sha256-71252f764fe9dfc25b3274620f2616129d328a69d51f9f7e370588683e2c36d3","01M6SD2EMRVEY7D3YTDZNZ63JC":"sha256-b7eb79acb68bdfba4ac49fc3d27c7659bfbf454ae6cb3d0dc410d93ad261301e","01M6SD2EMRZFN77T7878QZ49PQ":"sha256-771358ebe3e8265ba300d81d42309f27b0505de3adb9d1f20dedf0963c4c6daa"}}
